  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in. `npm test` passes: 177 tests, 0 failed, including the new ones.\n\n**Store (`src/store.js`)**\n- `reserve`, `confirm` and `release` follow your spec, as do the error codes and the expiry rule.\n- `getAvailable(sku)` is physical stock minus the quantities of active reservations. `getStock` still returns physical stock.\n- `removeItem` now checks against available stock, so it can't remove reserved units.\n- Time comes only from the store's `clock`.\n- `confirm` also returns `{sku, qty}`. The API uses that to build its response.\n\n**API (`src/api.js`)**\n- `GET /stock/:sku` now includes `available`.\n- `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` return the statuses you listed. The delete always returns `204` with a `null` body.\n- On `POST /reservations`, any error other than `INSUFFICIENT_STOCK` returns 400. On confirm, any error other than `RESERVATION_EXPIRED` returns 404.\n\n**Tests**\nI added store tests for reserve, expiry at exactly `creation + ttlMs`, confirm, release and `removeItem`. I added API tests for each endpoint's statuses.\n\n**Not specified, so I left it alone:**\n- **ttlMs:** it isn't validated.\n- **Expired reservations:** they stay in memory, which is how `confirm` can tell expired from unknown. They are never cleaned up.",
